A||||7||Dslice||Wiper Problem||||1||
Z||000000||Dslice||06-20-2001||09:38 PM||||Not sure but my stalk that contains the wiper controls on the steering wheel column might be bad. The Wipers turn on but don't like to stop and when they do its usually in the middle of the windshield. Also my wiper fluid button doesn't work but the pump does when I run a separate Pos wire to it.Is it safe to assume I'm right here?<P>Thanks,||||reg||1
Z||000001||kiss||06-20-2001||09:51 PM||||open your wiper motor, there is a module in there. replace it. only the dealer sells it!<BR>about $70.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||06-20-2001||10:22 PM||||If you replace the module in the wiper motor I would suggest trying to find one from a junker first.  <P>I have replaced the wiper switch on 2 cars which fixed a number of problems for me.  I would only use a new switch because it is such a pain to get to and replace.  Advance Auto sells the wiper switch for about $55 (GP Sorensen #DS170).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||BV MotorSports||06-20-2001||10:32 PM||||My 87 did the same thing a while back, changed out the electronics in the wiper motor and that problem went away. Now that I have her back on the road the wipers sometimes make a single swipe when I start the car. Thats kinda wierd. Anyone elses do that?<P>Steven||||reg||5
Z||000004||Devotshka||06-20-2001||11:17 PM||||It is extremely rare that the problem would lie in the wiper motor box (plug in board).  The cause for the random wipes and inability to turn the wipers off is in the wiper switch itself.  The switch is a tiny black box inside the steering column;  84s (possibly 85s) have 7 wires, later years have a three wire harness (purple, white, gray).  If you take your old one apart, you will see why your wipers have gotten a mind of their own... these pieces are horribly built.  I don't have the part # handy, but if you take your old one in, GM can match it for you to several other vehicles as well.... using one from later model bonnevilles will save you about $35 over using a fiero one... key difference, the newer ones click in between speed settings for delay.  Almost every fiero i've worked on has had this problem at one time or another, and replacing this part ALWAYS cures the problem.<P>On a side note, if the wiper board is in fact causing a problem, replacing the board in the motor is usually unnecessary.  Before you drop the cash for a new one, take your old one out and leave it in the sun for a bit.  Most of the time the gasket has failed on the cover and moisture has gotten in and shorted it out.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||BV MotorSports||06-20-2001||11:20 PM||||Thanks, very good info. Seems I will be picking up a new "black box" for a late model bonneville.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000006||Devotshka||06-20-2001||11:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BV MotorSports:<BR><B>Thanks, very good info. Seems I will be picking up a new "black box" for a late model bonneville.<P>Steven<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just be sure to match up the harness (you can see your old one without removing any more than the lower dash cover) to make sure it is 100% compatible.... some years have different connectors on the end that would need otherwise unnecessary splicing.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fieroluke||06-21-2001||03:04 AM||||Hi folks, here's my $0.02:<P>The most probable causes for the most common problems are:<P>* Wiper stops at random position when you turn it off (doesn't return to park): There is a switch inside the motor that's worn, NOT the board<BR>* Delay does not work: faulty board in wiper motor<BR>* Wiper comes on when you make a turn/drive over a bump: Faulty switch in steering column (intermittent in switch).<P><BR>Hope this helps,<P>-Oliver<P>------------------<BR>Visit my website: <A HREF="http://www.fieros.de" TARGET=_blank>www.fieros.de</A>  for lots of technical and other Fiero related information<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fieros.de/jpg/mycars.jpg"> ||||reg||4
